  {"date": "2014-07-13", "venue": "Randall's Island", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "What a difference an era makes.  Or not.  Mike surprises, early on, offering just a bit more.  Pushing through a few sour notes, Trey, playing with his feet almost as much as his hands, lays into an impassioned solo, offset by, no surprise, on-point Fish.  Of course Page is nearly front and center, and is right there to bring this Randall's Island play to a memorable close."},
